<title>UK: UK Unionists and SNP join forces to block air tax.</title>
<headline>UK Unionists and SNP join forces to block air tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Scottish Nationalist Party and the Ulster Unionists joined forces on Thursday to try to block the government's proposed doubling of its air passenger duty.</p>
<p>SNP leader Alex Salmond and Ulster Unionist leader David Trimble said they had written to other opposition parties asking for their support. Plaid Cymru leader, Dafydd Wigley, gave his immediate backing. But the Labour party was lukewarm.</p>
<p>A senior Labour source said it would review the SNP bid, but he did not expect to take a decision for at least a month.</p>
<p>The ruling Conservatives are currently at level pegging with all the opposition parties in parliament.</p>
</text>
